COMPILATION OF: E48C7

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E48C7

   1 a 0000 E48C7:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-48/P2c] THE STATIC-LEAK LAYOUT QUESTION: a flat CHARACTER STATIC declared
   4 a 0006 BEFORE an automatic record.  My binder propagates a level-0
   5 a 0006 storage class INTO every later structure unless the structure
   6 a 0006 names one -- manual 6.2 speaks of structure LEVELS, and DR's own
   7 a 0006 MPMCALLB declares `upper/lower static' at lines 48-50 and an
   8 a 0006 automatic `1 cpb' at 166 and compiles.  This object measures where
   9 a 0006 DR actually PLACES rec: automatic (above the pool, [C114]) or
  10 a 0006 static (below it).  The store inside is P2's member shape. */
  11 c 0006   dcl s char(3) static initial('AB');
  12 c 0006   dcl b bit(1) static initial('0'b);
  13 c 0006   dcl
  14 c 0006     1 rec,
  15 c 0006       2 name character(30) varying;
  16 c 0006   rec.name = 'AB';
  17 c 0013   b = (rec.name = 'EOF');
  18 c 0025   put list('S=', s);
  19 c 0047   put list('B=', b);
  20 c 0069   stop;
  21 a 006C end E48C7;

CODE SIZE = 006C
DATA AREA = 002C
FREE SYMS = 3854
END  COMPILATION
